## Expert Summary

An asscher cut diamond necklace is one of the most unusual pendants available. Most buyers default to round or oval. The step-cut pendant is rare — and the asscher's specific geometry makes it more visually distinct than an emerald cut at the same size.

The Step-Cut Pendant Effect makes quality selection non-negotiable. H-I color and SI1-SI2 clarity are visible in the asscher's Hall of Mirrors facets at neckline distance in a way they would not be in a round brilliant pendant. The flat step-cut planes are a window into the stone's quality.

The Lab Value Switch makes the buying decision easy — lab pendants deliver F-G color and VS2 clarity at $1,000–$3,820 for the full size range. Natural pendants deliver H-I/SI1-SI2 at $1,190–$6,640. Lab wins on quality and price simultaneously; the conventional natural-vs-lab trade-off does not exist in this catalog.

> **Farzana's take:** I love the asscher pendant for one reason: it is the most honest diamond pendant available. It does not hide behind sparkle. It shows what it is made of — literally, through those flat step-cut facets. That honesty is why the quality matters so much here. And it is why I always recommend lab for an asscher pendant. You are paying for a stone that will show itself clearly. Get a stone that looks good when it does.

